+## Built State
+(T001–T003, accepted 2026-07-26)
+
+`packages/orchestration/task_granularity.py` is a pure module — no
+filesystem, network, or environment access; thresholds arrive as a
+`GranularityConfig` argument. Its docstring states that v1 is heuristic on
+plan-intrinsic signals only, because no per-task cost history exists.
+
+`normalize_plan(plan, cfg)` returns the plan to use plus a list of
+`Transformation` records (`kind` split | merge | aborted |
+unsplittable_flag, `source_ids`, `result_ids`, `reason`):
+
+- **Split** — a task at or above the configured band, or above the
+  acceptance-count threshold, becomes one child per acceptance cluster.
+  Clusters group acceptance criteria by the `files_hint` entries they match
+  (token overlap, extension stripped); criteria that match no file each get
+  their own child. Children chain `depends_on`, the first inherits the
+  parent's, tasks that depended on the parent are rewired to the chain end,
+  and every child is band M with the reassignment marked heuristic. A task
+  with a single acceptance criterion, or whose criteria collapse into one
+  cluster, is left intact and recorded `unsplittable_flag`.
+- **Merge** — maximal runs of consecutive S-band tasks with few acceptance
+  criteria and overlapping `files_hint` tokens merge up to the group-size
+  cap, greedily left to right; titles join, acceptance concatenates,
+  `files_hint` unions, the band bumps one step. A group is refused when a
+  task outside it depends on a non-last member, or when contracting the
+  group would close a dependency cycle. Both refusals are recorded.
+- **Revalidation** — the new task list is materialized by constructing a new
+  `FlightPlan`, so the schema's own `_validate_dag` is the validator. A
+  construction failure returns the original plan plus a single `aborted`
+  record carrying the error: it fails open to the plan the human is about to
+  approve, never to a broken one.
+
+Four config keys drive it — `planning.granularity.enabled` (default true),
+`split_band` (XL), `max_acceptance` (3), `merge_group_size` (3) — each with
+a `REMEDY_PLANNING_GRANULARITY_*` env var. Disabled returns the original
+plan object and an empty record.
+
+Normalization runs at one insertion point, inside `plan_job_llm`, after the
+structured call validates. The record travels on
+`FlightPlanResult.transformations`, is persisted as
+`flight_plan["_normalization"]` by both call sites (initial plan and
+replan), and `render_plan_md` renders a **Normalization** section — listing
+each transformation, or stating that there were none — so the approving
+human always sees what changed. No Flight-Plan schema class was modified.
+
+`tests/orchestration/test_task_granularity.py` holds 26 tests: two
+parametrized tables (split and merge cases), the mixed acceptance fixture
+checked against a golden record, determinism plus a fixed-point re-run,
+byte-identical pass-through when disabled, and the revalidation abort.
+Wiring and rendering are covered in `tests/orchestration/test_flight_plan.py`
+and `tests/cli/test_plan_approval.py`.
